# diffy engineering process (SPEC.md §14)

All development in this repo is test-driven. `SPEC.md` is the source of truth.

- Red-green-refactor: write a failing test encoding the spec'd behavior
  BEFORE any implementation. If the spec is silent, amend SPEC.md first.
- Test names cite the spec section, e.g.
  `replay_preserves_spans_through_partial_edit_6_1`.
- No implementation commit without its preceding failing test.
- Every module gets `//!` docs naming its spec section; every public item
  gets `///` docs; non-obvious logic comments explain WHY, citing SPEC.md
  sections.
- Invariants are commented where enforced: I1–I4 (evidence only,
  conservation via git diffs, immutable inputs, fail-closed) in rewrite
  code; byte-identity at the replay engine's entry point.
- Integration tests use real git repos in tempdirs; never mock git.
- Done = tests green + spec section marked implemented + `cargo doc` clean.
